# FIXED 2026-08-26 (the preference admission gate, ADR-004).
# expected: 'autoo' refused -- it is not a member of the enum disjunction
# actual (now matches): [aontu/empty] at $.k, exit 1 -- an override
#         must be admitted by an alternative or equal the preferred
#         value, so *A|B|C is a true enum-with-default; unset still
#         generates "auto" and k:'literal' still overrides. Pinned by
#         test/spec/pref.tsv pref-admit-enum-nonmember-refused.
#         (Old behaviour: {"k":"autoo"} exit 0 -- the same-kind
#         override replaced the pref with no alternative consulted.)
k: *'auto' | 'literal' | 'data'
k: 'autoo'
